pokeplatinum-widepointers9.patch (tools/pokeplat_gen.py applies it to build/pokeplatinum, after widepointers8.patch): battle_subscreen.c's
GetTargetSlotFlags and GetBattlerTargetFlags count their output flags with SNELEMS(outFlags), where outFlags is a `u8 *` parameter:
sizeof of the pointer, 4 bytes on the DS (so 4 flags, the size of every caller's u8[4]) and 8 on the 64-bit host. In a double battle's
target menu the loop wrote 8 flags into the 4-byte buffer (it overwrote the caller's saved btlSubscreen pointer with 0x01 bytes: SIGSEGV
in GetBattlerTargetFlags from BattleSubscreen_DrawTargetSelectBg) and read battlersByType[6..9], past its 6 entries. The count is now the
constant 4. Found by the Jubilife tag battle (route pt leg galactic); tools/plat_lint.py's C5 (-Wsizeof-pointer-div) finds this class in
the whole tree: these two lines were the only hits.
diff --git a/src/battle/battle_subscreen.c b/src/battle/battle_subscreen.c
--- a/src/battle/battle_subscreen.c
+++ b/src/battle/battle_subscreen.c
@@ -2565,4 +2565,7 @@
 }
 
+// outFlags is a u8[4] in every caller; SNELEMS(outFlags) on the pointer parameter was 4 on the DS and 8 on the host
+#define TARGET_FLAG_COUNT 4
+
 static void GetTargetSlotFlags(BattleSubscreen *btlSubscreen, u8 *outFlags, BOOL checkPresence)
 {
@@ -2572,5 +2575,5 @@
     BattleSystem_SetBattlersByType(btlSubscreen->battleSys, battlersByType);
 
-    for (int i = 0; i < SNELEMS(outFlags); i++) {
+    for (int i = 0; i < TARGET_FLAG_COUNT; i++) {
         int battlerIdx = battlersByType[2 + i];
 
@@ -2591,5 +2594,5 @@
     case 10:
     case 11:
-        for (int i = 0; i < SNELEMS(outFlags); i++) {
+        for (int i = 0; i < TARGET_FLAG_COUNT; i++) {
             if (i == selectedTarget - 1) {
                 outFlags[i] = TRUE;
